dialogue cave_party_talk
title: Where the light goes
trigger: ThemeStart cave
speaker commander $commander
speaker trusted $trusted
speaker smith - name=Blacksmith portrait=tinkerer

node a commander
  The wraith knights lowered their blades to me, then fought us anyway. And this arch hummed awake as I passed. What is it holding up?
  -> b

node b smith
  Nothing. The Street's engineer read the arch you woke: it's a tap, not a support. It draws the Manalith's mana down, and the drawing is the pull that brings it closer. The Watch knew you for one of Halcyon's. They saluted their own.
  * You looked at me differently when the Watch saluted. Tell me why. -> speak
    if: TrustAtLeast $trusted 25
  * Halcyon's, then. I'd still rather know than guess.

node speak trusted
  Because they saluted, and I didn't know if I should. Halcyon put the Manalith to sleep and drank the spill. Maybe you were one of them. I know who you've been out here. That's the one I'm following.
  * Keep judging me by what I do out here. Hold me to it. -> hold
    do: AddTrust $trusted 6
  * I don't know what I was either. I'm glad you're still here. -> glad
    do: AddTrust $trusted 4

node hold trusted
  I will. Every day, if I have to.

node glad trusted
  Still here. Ask me again after the next arch.
